' --- manual: everything below this line is hand-authored; the script preserves it ---

ores.shell.api ..> ores.shell.workflow : menu, command feedback, argument parsing
ores.workflow.api ..> ores.shell.workflow : domain, messaging

' The automated pass draws one box per unit and cannot show which a person wrote,
' or why. Two are generated from the workflow entity models, one per entity, and
' answer its derived verbs. workflow_operations_commands is generated from the
' operation model ores.workflow.workflow_messages. workflow_run_commands is
' hand-written, because wait and start do work around their messages that no model
' states. Bundles, provision and ORE import call its wait_for_instance.

note bottom of "ores::shell::app::commands::workflow::workflow_run_commands"
Answers `workflow wait` and `workflow start`, the two workflow
verbs that are not messages: wait polls a run, and start publishes
on the stream with no reply. It joins the workflow menu that the
generated workflow_operations_commands owns, and exposes
wait_for_instance for the command units that dispatch a workflow
and then block on it.
end note

